# Documentation

Document knowledge, not activity. Do not write down what the code, a test or the git history
already says. When a change makes knowledge outdated, update it in the same PR as the code.

## Protected files

Feature branches never modify `docs/project/changelog.md`, `docs/project/progress.md` or
`docs/product/roadmap.md`. A dedicated `chore/docs` PR updates them after each merge batch
(`CLAUDE.md`).

## Where each kind of knowledge lives

The standard is `docs/adr/0006-comment-and-documentation-standard.md`.

| Document                           | Holds                                                                                      | Update it when                                     |
| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |
| Code comments                      | module headers, TSDoc contracts, "why" comments with their source                          | always, in the same commit as the code             |
| `CONTEXT.md`                       | the ubiquitous-language glossary, by context                                               | you add, rename or redefine a domain term          |
| `docs/adr/NNNN-<slug>.md`          | decisions, MADR 4 format, indexed in `docs/adr/README.md`                                  | a decision meets the tests in `docs/adr/README.md` |
| `docs/engineering/architecture.md` | context map, C4 container view, layers, entry points, where code goes                      | a context, a layer rule or an entry point changes  |
| `src/modules/<context>/README.md`  | technical doc of one context: responsibilities, public API, data flow, invariants, diagram | the context's API, flows or invariants change      |
| `docs/functional/<context>.md`     | functional doc of one context: what the player can do, the rules, the edge cases           | player-visible behaviour of the context changes    |
| `docs/product/user-guide.md`       | the guide for players                                                                      | a user-visible feature is added or changed         |

A context's README and functional doc are created by the PR that creates its `src/modules/<context>/`
folder. The comment standard, with templates, is `docs/engineering/code-documentation.md`.

## Rules

- English only, plain and precise: short sentences, active voice, no hype.
- One fact, one place. Link to it instead of copying it.
- Cite sources: the CR number for a game rule, a URL and the date read for an external limit, the
  ADR or PR number for a decision.
- Fix or delete every comment and doc sentence your change made false, in the same commit.
- No changelog entries, "Last updated" stamps or progress checkboxes in feature PRs.
- Diagrams are Mermaid blocks in Markdown.
- Run Prettier on the Markdown you change.
- List the docs you touched in the PR template's "Docs touched" section.
